402	110,515,1105,1340	402. Flowers of Cichory, all with strap-shaped corollas.	A flowering sprig of Cichory: one head open flat with many strap-shaped, square-toothed rays around a tuft of styles, a half-open head above, and a bud at the tip.
403	465,1540,1650,2012	403. Head of Cichory-flowers, divided lengthwise and enlarged.	A Cichory head cut down the middle: strap-shaped corollas spreading out to each side, the upright tubes and curled styles of the flowers crowded in the centre on the dotted receptacle.
